Package: ff802-cc-auto
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Bernhard Steinheber <bernhard@steinheber.info>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libusb-1.0-0 (>= 2:1.0.22), libasound2t64 (>= 1.2.10), systemd, udev
Recommends: pkexec, libnotify-bin
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Description: automatic class-compliant mode for the RME Fireface 802
 Switches an original RME Fireface 802 (not the 802 FS) that is connected
 in proprietary USB mode (2a39:3fcd) to class-compliant mode by sending
 the CC enable command (01 00 44 BD) once per USB connection and then
 resetting the USB hub port of exactly this unit, as "ff802-cc enable" does
 (no reconnecting needed). If the port cannot be reset, it asks the
 user in the Plasma session to reconnect the USB cable. Afterwards the
 unit appears as 0424:3fdd and uses the ff802-ucm-profile configuration.
 .
 The automation is off after installation: ff802-cc-auto on (administrator)
 turns it on, ff802-cc-auto off (active local user) turns it off,
 ff802-cc-auto status shows the state. The package never switches the unit
 back to proprietary mode; for that use "ff802-cc disable" of the separate
 package ff802-cc, TotalMix FX on Windows/macOS or the ARC.
 .
 Optional, also off after installation and independent of the automation:
 ff802-cc-auto mixer-init on sets, on every connection in class-compliant
 mode, the routings Playback 1/2 -> Phones 9/10 (set by the class-compliant
 mode) off and the routings Playback 1..12 -> Output 1..12 and the volumes
 of the twelve hardware outputs to 0 dB through the ALSA sequencer (MIDI
 port 2 of the unit), 26 register writes. Other crossed routings and
 input routings are not cleared. ff802-mixer-init --dry-run|--apply runs
 the same initialisation once by hand.
